# Graph Ownership Boundary

All PreBase-owned Architecture Graph and Network Graph implementation must live under the repository root folder named exactly `graphs/`.

This includes code, styles, tests, fixtures, scripts, settings definitions, commands, host adapters, Magnus graph tools (implementation owned by graphs), diagnostics, and graph documentation.

Generic VS Code services (files, workspace, editor, configuration, webview infrastructure) may remain outside `graphs/`. PreBase adapters that connect those services to graphs are graph-owned and belong under `graphs/`.

A minimal host bootstrap outside `graphs/` is allowed only when required by the workbench entrypoint. It must contain no graph logic/state/settings/rendering/business rules, only register/import the graph package, and must be listed in the graph-boundary allowlist.

Before adding a graph file elsewhere, document why it is generic infrastructure rather than graph-owned.

Enforce with `graphs/scripts/verify-boundary/` (see `graphs/OWNERSHIP.md` for interim legacy paths under `src/vs/workbench/contrib/prebase/` until BETA-001 migration completes).
